Description: glsnake: three places for the second light, taking turns
 Before glsnake-light-position.patch, the second light's place came from
 uninitialised memory, so users saw three different pictures from launch to
 launch: the light at the viewer (most launches), the sun shining from the
 authors' direction, or a lamp. That patch keeps the light at the viewer;
 this one lets the user have all three.
 .
 Light 1 can be at the viewer (0, 0, 0, 1), the lamp where the authors placed
 it (0, 20, -1, 1), or the sun from that direction (0, 20, -1, 0). Each has a
 switch (--viewer-light, --lamp-light, --sun-light and their --no- forms), an
 X resource (viewerLight, lampLight, sunLight, all True) and a checkbox in
 the settings (hacks/config/glsnake.xml, labels translated in de, fr, ja, ko,
 pl, pt_BR, zh_CN and zh_TW). The lights switched on take turns, the next one
 whenever start_morph() begins a new shape, starting with the viewer; one
 switched on stays; with none on, all three take turns. Light 0 is unchanged.
 The position is set in gl_init(), which the draw path calls every frame with
 the identity modelview, as before.
 .
 This is a Sparky Stereo OS choice made by Daniel Ramos, not a request to
 upstream.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
